  PlaceName: Ruby's Place
  Icon: {fileID: -3103549794962549916, guid: ec459ca310d2bb947a7ec8cf7cdc490f, type: 3}
  Color: {r: 1, g: 0.6862745, b: 0.50980395, a: 1}
  Content: '"The Story So Far"

    Claire Gallagher

    An excerpt from a graphic
    novel in progress, set in a fictional 1960s mining town. It explores Northern
    isolation, queerness, and the fine line between human and monstrous.


    "Re:
    Unicorn"

    Abigail Clapper and Grace Hirsch

    Three large-scale illustrated
    paper works reimagine mythical creatures through themes of labour, movement,
    and nostalgia. The adaptable installation evokes stories of healing and rediscovery."


    "Athabaskan
    Style: Pre-Contact Stories and Designs"

    Shadunjen van Kampen

    Watercolour
    paintings inspired by ancient Athabaskan artistic traditions. This exhibit reclaims
    visual stories often lost in the dominant culture."

'
  RavenSucessScript: "\u201CThree stories, one nest: memory, myth, and medicine.
    You\u2019ve stepped into a house of quiet rebellions and reclaimed wonder.\u201D"
  RavenHintScript: "\u201CHeard whispers about a hidden vault? Finish your round
    to see what squawks back.\u201D"
